A consumer that stages the binary needs to know whether *this* build can run its
gate, which a version cannot answer. `--require` asserts a capability by name.

Five kinds, and all five are exercised here on purpose: the defect this flag
already had was accepting output formats and evidence kinds while its help named
only the other three, so a corpus that checks three would have reproduced it
(`A1-093`).

```
$ aplan facts --require test.covers_by_test --require APLAN024 --require tasks --require sarif --require commit
aplan [..] advertises every required capability (5 checked)

```

A widening of an existing rule is assertable too, which a rule code cannot express:
`--require APLAN008` passes on every build since that rule existed, long before it learned to
resolve a table row (`A1-099`).

```
$ aplan facts --require traces.table_rows
aplan [..] advertises every required capability (1 checked)

```

Every missing one is named, not just the first: fixing them one build at a time
is the slow version of what this command is for.

```
$ aplan facts --require deny_warnings --require APLAN099 --require nope
? 1
aplan [..] does not advertise:
  APLAN099
  nope
It advertises [..] others; `aplan facts` lists them. A build that predates `--require` refuses the flag instead, and exits 2.

```

Anything the build advertises can be asserted, which includes an output format
and an evidence kind, not only the three above.

```
$ aplan facts --require sarif --require commit
aplan [..] advertises every required capability (2 checked)

```

One capability named twice is one question, and a blank one is not a question at
all.

```
$ aplan facts --require APLAN024 --require APLAN024
aplan [..] advertises every required capability (1 checked)

```

```
$ aplan facts --require ""
? 2
aplan: `--require` needs a capability name; one was empty

```

The two failures stay apart on purpose. A build that answers "no" exits 1; a
build too old to be asked has no such flag and exits 2, so an operator is never
told a binary lacks a key it actually supports.

```
$ aplan facts --requires nope
? 2
error: unexpected argument '--requires' found

  tip: a similar argument exists: '--require'

Usage: aplan facts --require <CAPABILITY>

For more information, try '--help'.

```
